From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 23:45:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 190/342] arm64: a cache maintenance fault is a read

A data abort from a cache maintenance instruction (DC CVAU, IC IVAU)
always has ESR's WnR bit set, and the CM bit says where it came from;
the instruction needs only read access. The handler took WnR alone, so
when such an instruction touched a page of a read-only area that wasn't
mapped yet, vm_page_fault() saw a write to a read-only page and the team
got SIGSEGV. LLVM's JIT (llvmpipe) does exactly that: it writes code,
makes the memory read-only and executable, then cleans it with
__clear_cache(), and gltest's texture scene crashed in
llvm::sys::Memory::InvalidateInstructionCache().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/arch_int.cpp | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/arch_int.cpp b/src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/arch_int.cpp
index bf2d7a96e1..6e9b2ecd2d 100644
--- a/src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/arch_int.cpp
+++ b/src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/arch_int.cpp
@@ -318,7 +318,11 @@ do_sync_handler(iframe * frame)
 		case EXCP_DATA_ABORT_L:
 		case EXCP_DATA_ABORT:
 		{
-			bool write = (frame->esr & ISS_DATA_WnR) != 0;
+			// a cache maintenance instruction (DC CVAU, IC IVAU...) always
+			// reports WnR, but needs only read access: JIT compilers clean
+			// the code they wrote after making it read-only and executable
+			bool write = (frame->esr & ISS_DATA_WnR) != 0
+				&& (frame->esr & ISS_DATA_CM) == 0;
 			bool known = false;
 
 			int initialLevel = VMSAv8TranslationMap::CalcStartLevel(48, 12);
